[gd_scene load_steps=26 format=3]

; THE FIDELITY SHOWCASE — one dark room, lit only by practicals you can see.
;
; This is the Isolation benchmark, composed. Everything the milestone built is
; standing in it at once: the gobo library on three fixtures, all three material
; families, all three hero props, and the game's own environment (AgX at 0.78,
; volumetric fog at 0.030, SSR, SSIL, the 1.65 glow threshold) unmodified.
;
; THE RULE THE SCENE IS BUILT AROUND: every light in here is a fixture the
; player can walk up to and point at. There is no key light hanging in the void,
; no fill, no ambient cheat beyond the environment's own near-black. If a corner
; is dark it is because nobody put a lamp there. That is DESIGN.md pillar 2 and
; pillar 6 enforced at the same time, and it is the only way a room can look
; photographed rather than lit.
;
; The five sources, and what justifies each:
;   1. TRIPOD WORK LIGHT (warm 3050 K, vent-slat gobo). Somebody is servicing
;      the coolant stack against the left wall. They brought a lamp, ran a cable
;      to a battery block, opened a toolbox, and have not come back.
;   2. DUCT APERTURE (cold 6200 K, drip-grate gobo, behind a real slatted
;      grille). A service run above the ceiling that still has power. Its light
;      falls through the grating as the room's one hero shaft.
;   3. BACKLIT SLAT PANEL, wall (emissive-only fallback). A fixture whose
;      ballast is dead — it glows and it does not light. In frame beside a
;      working one, on purpose: this is the graceful degrade being photographed
;      rather than described.
;   4. BACKLIT SLAT PANEL, under-counter (real AreaLight3D). The comms desk's
;      task light, washing the floor in front of the console.
;   5. CRT TERMINALS, three of them, the middle one retrofitted with a textured
;      AreaLight3D. The comms-room reference in one object.
;
; TWO CAMERAS, one per reference frame:
;   CamSlats   — "work light through slats in haze". Shoot the beam side-on so
;                the volumetric does the work and the slats break over the
;                machinery in front of the wall.
;   CamScreens — "screens casting green light". The console, its phosphor cast,
;                the under-counter wash, and gold lagging to carry the specular.
;
;   tools/fidelity_bench/shoot.sh res://tools/fidelity_bench/showcase.tscn \
;       <out>.png 1920x1080 240 CamSlats
;   tools/fidelity_bench/shoot.sh res://tools/fidelity_bench/showcase.tscn \
;       <out>.png 1920x1080 240 CamScreens

[ext_resource type="Environment" path="res://src/world/layer_environment.tres" id="1_env"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/props/fidelity/work_light.tscn" id="2_worklight"]
[ext_resource type="PackedScene" path="res://assets/props/fidelity/slat_diffuser_panel.tscn" id="3_panel"]
